the taliban first emerged in the early  1990s pledging to improve security and  fight corruption in afghanistan  fearing its religious traditions were  under threat it also promised to protect  them at any cost enforcing its version  of islamic law  its fighters had been poorly equipped at  times but highly motivated by their  mission to declare what they call an  islamic emirate of afghanistan the  taliban controlled much of the country  from 1996 to 2001. the armed group was  familiar with afghanistan's rugged  terrain and used this knowledge to  outsmart its enemies  when u.s forces overthrew the taliban 20  years ago it managed to survive and  continued to launch attacks against  afghan forces and their western allies  when it was in power members of the  taliban carried out public executions  and amputations commanders banned women  from working girls from going to school  and listening to or playing music  taliban leaders say they recognize the  society has changed and they've promised  to respect people's rights  before we didn't have as much  responsibility as we do today because  now we are all tested by god day by day  we will get involved in the service of  our nation in providing them with  security and hope for their future  largely funded by taxing landowners and  opium the taliban has been welcomed in  some areas of the country while despised  and feared in others  the legitimacy the armed group wanted  was denied time and again but peace  negotiations in qatar's capital gave it  a seat at the table  now with the taliban fully in control of  afghanistan the world is watching and  waiting to see how it will govern the  country and its people osama bin laden
 

